*==============================================================================
* FDOPAMP_FULL - behavioural fully differential op-amp macromodel (ngspice, LTspice)
*
* Copyright (c) 2026 Stanislav Maslovski
* SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause  (see LICENSE)
* Version 1.3 (2026-11). Developed with the help of Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic).
*
* Pins: inp inn vcc vee outp outn vocm
*   outp is the non-inverted output (in phase with inp), outn the inverted one.
*   vocm sets the output common-mode voltage. Left open, it floats to
*   mid-supply through an internal divider (2*RVOCM to each rail).
*
* DIFFERENTIAL-MODE (DM) PATH  (same structure as OPAMP_FULL)
*   - DC gain A0, dominant pole, GBW, two extra poles (FP2, FP3)
*   - input stage tanh() -> differential output slew rate SR
*   - input CM range window, input R/C, optional differential clamp
*     (anti-parallel diodes between inp and inn; no clamps to the rails)
*   - VOS, IB/IOS, CMRR(f), PSRR(f), white + 1/f voltage noise, white + 1/f
*     current noise (FCIN = 1/f corner, independent on each input; 0 = off)
* COMMON-MODE (CM) LOOP  (internal CMFB)
*   - senses the output CM (V(outp)+V(outn))/2 and compares it with V(vocm)
*   - CM error amplifier: DC gain A0CM, unity-gain frequency GBWCM, second
*     pole FPCM2, output CM slew rate SRCM, CM offset VOSCM
*   - CMRR, PSRR and the DM gain do not affect it (ideal CM/DM separation)
* OUTPUT STAGES (one per output, as in OPAMP_FULL)
*   - V(outp) = Vcm + Vd/2, V(outn) = Vcm - Vd/2 behind ROUT each
*   - swing limits VHD/VLD, current limits ISRC/ISNK, crossover VXO, COUT
*   - supply current = quiescent + load currents from the right rail
*
* Defaults approximate a generic +/-5 V, 100 MHz bipolar FDA.
* Units: SR, SRCM in V/s. CMRR/PSRR as ratios (31.6k = 90 dB).
*
* Notes
*   - SR is the DIFFERENTIAL output slew rate (each output slews at SR/2).
*   - The DM node n1 holds the differential output voltage. It is clamped to
*     +/-2*min(V(vcc)-VHD-Vocm, Vocm-V(vee)-VLD), so the outputs saturate
*     symmetrically and recover quickly.
*   - FDOPAMP_CORE exposes the single-ended CM control path through the pins
*     cmo (CM amplifier output) and cmi (output-stage CM input), so that the
*     CM loop can be opened for loop-gain tests. FDOPAMP_FULL joins them.
*   - Portability (v1.3): tested in ngspice-42 and LTspice 26 (identical
*     DC/AC/transient/noise results). White e_n is passed through the E
*     source Ewn (LTspice ignores the noise of a resistor that is read only
*     inside a B-source expression). Nodes that otherwise see only G
*     elements and capacitors get a 1e15 ohm DC path to ground (R*lk), which
*     satisfies the floating-node checks of LTspice/PSpice; their effect on
*     gain and noise is negligible. PSpice/HSPICE need a port (no B sources).
*
* PARAMETERS  (name, unit, default, meaning)
*  Gain and frequency response
*   A0      V/V    100k     open-loop DC gain
*   GBW     Hz     100Meg   gain-bandwidth product (unity-gain frequency of the
*                           dominant-pole response)
*   FP2     Hz     300Meg   second pole
*   FP3     Hz     1G       third pole
*   SR      V/s    200Meg   slew rate of the DIFFERENTIAL output
*                           (each output slews at SR/2)
*  Input DC errors and impedance
*   VOS     V      1m       input offset voltage, in series with the + input
*   IB      A      2u       input bias current (average of the two pins);
*                           IB > 0 flows into the pins (NPN), IB < 0 out (PNP)
*   IOS     A      0.1u     input offset current, I(inp) - I(inn)
*   RID     ohm    1Meg     differential input resistance (noiseless)
*   CID     F      1p       differential input capacitance
*   RIC     ohm    200Meg   common-mode input resistance of each input pin to
*                           ground (noiseless)
*   CIC     F      1p       common-mode input capacitance of each input pin to
*                           ground
*  Differential input clamp (two anti-parallel diodes between inp and inn;
*  there are no clamp diodes from the inputs to the supply rails)
*   VCLMP   V      100      forward voltage of each diode at 1 mA (set through
*                           the emission coefficient); 100 = no clamp.
*                           OP27-style clamp: VCLMP=0.7 RCLMP=100
*   RCLMP   ohm    100      series resistance of each clamp diode
*  Common-mode and supply rejection
*   CMRR    ratio  31.6k    DC CMRR (31.6k = 90 dB)
*   FCMRR   Hz     100k     CMRR falls at 20 dB/dec above this frequency
*   PSRRP   ratio  10k      DC rejection of the positive supply
*   PSRRN   ratio  10k      DC rejection of the negative supply
*   FPSRR   Hz     100k     PSRR falls at 20 dB/dec above this frequency
*   VCCN    V      5        nominal positive supply (PSRR reference)
*   VEEN    V      -5       nominal negative supply (PSRR reference)
*   VCMN    V      mid      input CM voltage at which VOS is specified; the
*                           CMRR error is (Vcm - VCMN)/CMRR
*  Noise
*   ENOISE  V/rtHz 5n       white input voltage noise density
*   FCEN    Hz     1k       1/f corner of the voltage noise
*   INOISE  A/rtHz 1p       white input current noise density, each input
*   FCIN    Hz     0        1/f corner of the current noise (independent on
*                           the two inputs); 0 = white only
*  Supplies, input range and output swing
*   ICCQ    A      10m      quiescent supply current, vcc to vee
*   ICMHI   V      1.5      input CM range: distance below vcc at which the
*                           input-stage gm has fallen to half (< 0: beyond rail)
*   ICMLO   V      1        the same, above vee
*   VK      V      0.1      width of the gm roll-off at the input-range edges
*   VHD     V      1.2      minimum headroom, output to vcc (swing limit)
*   VLD     V      1.2      minimum headroom, output to vee (swing limit)
*  Output stage (per output)
*   ROUT    ohm    10       output resistance
*   COUT    F      1p       output capacitance to ground
*   ISRC    A      50m      maximum source current
*   ISNK    A      50m      maximum sink current
*   VXO     V      0        class-AB crossover dead zone: for |Iout| below about
*                           VXO/ROUT the small-signal output resistance is
*                           2*ROUT; 0 disables it
*  Common-mode loop and vocm pin (FDA only)
*   A0CM    V/V    10k      DC gain of the CM error amplifier
*   GBWCM   Hz     50Meg    unity-gain frequency of the CM error amplifier
*   FPCM2   Hz     200Meg   second pole of the CM loop
*   SRCM    V/s    100Meg   slew rate of the output CM voltage
*   VOSCM   V      1m       output CM offset: Vout,cm = V(vocm) + VOSCM
*   RVOCM   ohm    50k      vocm pin bias: 2*RVOCM (noiseless) to each rail,
*                           i.e. RVOCM to mid-supply when the pin is open
*   CVOCM   F      1p       vocm pin capacitance to ground
*==============================================================================

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* FDZCPL : out = K * (1 + s/(2*pi*FZ)) * in   (same as ZCPL in opamp_full.lib)
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt FDZCPL in out PARAMS: K=1u FZ=1k FHI=2G
.param TAUZ={1/(6.283185307*FZ)} CD=1n
Ek  na 0 in 0 {K}
Cd  in nx {CD}
Gd  nx nv nx nv {6.283185307*FHI*CD}
Vs  nv 0 0
Rlk nx 0 1e15
Hd  out na Vs {K*TAUZ/CD}
.ends FDZCPL

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt FDOPAMP_CORE inp inn vcc vee outp outn vocm cmo cmi
+ PARAMS:
+ A0=100k GBW=100Meg SR=200Meg FP2=300Meg FP3=1G
+ VOS=1m IB=2u IOS=0.1u
+ RID=1Meg CID=1p RIC=200Meg CIC=1p
+ CMRR=31.6k FCMRR=100k PSRRP=10k PSRRN=10k FPSRR=100k VCCN=5 VEEN=-5
+ VCMN={0.5*(VCCN+VEEN)}
+ ENOISE=5n FCEN=1k INOISE=1p FCIN=0
+ ICCQ=10m VHD=1.2 VLD=1.2 ICMHI=1.5 ICMLO=1 VK=0.1
+ ROUT=10 ISRC=50m ISNK=50m VXO=0 COUT=1p
+ VCLMP=100 RCLMP=100
+ A0CM=10k GBWCM=50Meg FPCM2=200Meg SRCM=100Meg VOSCM=1m
+ RVOCM=50k CVOCM=1p

* ---- derived constants -------------------------------------------------------
.param PI2=6.283185307
.param C1V=1p
.param IMAXV={SR*C1V}
.param GM0={PI2*GBW*C1V}
.param R1V={A0/GM0}
.param ICMV={SRCM*C1V}
.param GMC={PI2*GBWCM*C1V}
.param RCV={A0CM/GMC}
.param VNTH={sqrt(4*1.380649e-23*300.15*1e3)}
.param IFL=10m
.param VTN={1.380649e-23*300.15/1.602176634e-19}
.param KFV={ENOISE*ENOISE*FCEN*IFL/(VTN*VTN)}
.param ESH2={4*1.602176634e-19*VTN*VTN/IFL}
.param GENV={sqrt(max(ENOISE*ENOISE-ESH2,0))/VNTH}
.param GNI={INOISE/VNTH}
* 1/f current noise (FCIN > 0): one more flicker diode pair per input, so the
* two pins get independent noise. The flicker voltage of the pair is scaled to
* VNI*sqrt(FCIN/f) with VNI = 1 uV/rtHz and converted to current by GFI =
* INOISE/VNI, giving INOISE^2*FCIN/f. The pair's shot noise then adds only
* (0.21n/1u)^2 = 4e-8 of INOISE^2. FCIN = 0 disables the sources (GFI = 0).
.param KFI={1e-12*FCIN*IFL/(VTN*VTN)}
.param GFI={FCIN>0 ? INOISE/1u : 0}

* ---- input network (noiseless; RID behind the series error voltage) ----------
Gid  inp inn vd 0 {1/RID}
Cid  inp inn {CID}
Gic1 inp 0 inp 0 {1/RIC}
Gic2 inn 0 inn 0 {1/RIC}
Cic1 inp 0 {CIC}
Cic2 inn 0 {CIC}
Ibp  inp 0 DC {IB+IOS/2}
Ibn  inn 0 DC {IB-IOS/2}
Dp1  inp inn DIN
Dp2  inn inp DIN
.model DIN D(IS=1e-15 N={VCLMP/(VTN*log(1e-3/1e-15))} RS={RCLMP})

* ---- noise sources -------------------------------------------------------------
Rnv  nnv 0 1e3
Ewn  nwn 0 nnv 0 {GENV}
Rnp  nnp 0 1e3
Rnn  nnn 0 1e3
Gnp  0 inp nnp 0 {GNI}
Gnn  0 inn nnn 0 {GNI}
Ifa  0 nfa DC {IFL}
Dfa  nfa 0 DFLK
Ifb  0 nfb DC {IFL}
Dfb  nfb 0 DQ
Efl  nfl 0 nfa nfb 1
.model DFLK D(IS=1e-14 N=1 KF={KFV} AF=1)
.model DQ   D(IS=1e-14 N=1)
* 1/f current noise, independent on each input (FCIN > 0)
Ifp1 0 nfp1 DC {IFL}
Dfp1 nfp1 0 DFLKI
Ifp2 0 nfp2 DC {IFL}
Dfp2 nfp2 0 DQ
Gfp  0 inp nfp1 nfp2 {GFI}
Ifn1 0 nfn1 DC {IFL}
Dfn1 nfn1 0 DFLKI
Ifn2 0 nfn2 DC {IFL}
Dfn2 nfn2 0 DQ
Gfn  0 inn nfn1 nfn2 {GFI}
.model DFLKI D(IS=1e-14 N=1 KF={KFI} AF=1)

* ---- CMRR and PSRR coupling into the DM input ----------------------------------
Bcm  ncm0 0 V = 0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn))-{VCMN}
Xcm  ncm0 ncm FDZCPL PARAMS: K={1/CMRR} FZ={FCMRR}
Bps1 nps1i 0 V = V(vcc)-{VCCN}
Xps1 nps1i nps1 FDZCPL PARAMS: K={1/PSRRP} FZ={FPSRR}
Bps2 nps2i 0 V = V(vee)-{VEEN}
Xps2 nps2i nps2 FDZCPL PARAMS: K={1/PSRRN} FZ={FPSRR}

Bvd  vd 0 V = V(inp)-V(inn)+{VOS}+V(ncm)+V(nps1)+V(nps2)+V(nwn)+V(nfl)
Bwin nwin 0 V = max(0.25*(1+tanh((0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn))-V(vee)-{ICMLO})/{VK}))*(1+tanh((V(vcc)-{ICMHI}-0.5*(V(inp)+V(inn)))/{VK})),1e-3)

* ---- DM gain node: n1 = differential output voltage ---------------------------
Bgm  0 n1 I = {IMAXV}*V(nwin)*tanh({GM0}*V(vd)/{IMAXV})
G1   n1 0 n1 0 {1/R1V}
C1   n1 0 {C1V}
R1lk n1 0 1e15
* symmetric differential swing limit set by the headroom around Vocm
Bdlim ndl 0 V = max(2*min(V(vcc)-{VHD}-V(vocm), V(vocm)-V(vee)-{VLD}), 10m)
Bclp n1 0 I = {IMAXV/1e-3}*(max(V(n1)-V(ndl),0)+min(V(n1)+V(ndl),0))
G2   0 n2 n1 0 1m
G2r  n2 0 n2 0 1m
C2   n2 0 {1/(PI2*FP2*1e3)}
R2lk n2 0 1e15
G3   0 n3 n2 0 1m
G3r  n3 0 n3 0 1m
C3   n3 0 {1/(PI2*FP3*1e3)}
R3lk n3 0 1e15

* ---- Vocm pin: noiseless divider to mid-supply ------------------------------------
Gvo1 vcc vocm vcc vocm {1/(2*RVOCM)}
Gvo2 vocm vee vocm vee {1/(2*RVOCM)}
Cvo  vocm 0 {CVOCM}

* ---- CM loop: error amplifier (integrator + pole) -----------------------------
Bocs nocs 0 V = 0.5*(V(outp)+V(outn))
Bgmc 0 nc1 I = {ICMV}*tanh({GMC}*(V(vocm)+{VOSCM}-V(nocs))/{ICMV})
Gc1  nc1 0 nc1 0 {1/RCV}
Cc1  nc1 0 {C1V}
Rc1lk nc1 0 1e15
Bchi nchi 0 V = V(vcc)-{VHD}
Bclo nclo 0 V = V(vee)+{VLD}
Bcclp nc1 0 I = {ICMV/1e-3}*(max(V(nc1)-V(nchi),0)+min(V(nc1)-V(nclo),0))
Gc2  0 cmo nc1 0 1m
Gc2r cmo 0 cmo 0 1m
Cc2  cmo 0 {1/(PI2*FPCM2*1e3)}
Rc2lk cmo 0 1e15

* ---- output stages ----------------------------------------------------------------
Bdp  ndp 0 V = V(cmi)+0.5*V(n3)
Bdn  ndn 0 V = V(cmi)-0.5*V(n3)
Bicp nicp 0 V = min({ISRC},max(-{ISNK},((V(ndp)-V(outp))-0.5*{VXO}*tanh((V(ndp)-V(outp))/({VXO}+1e-9)))/{ROUT}))
Bicn nicn 0 V = min({ISRC},max(-{ISNK},((V(ndn)-V(outn))-0.5*{VXO}*tanh((V(ndn)-V(outn))/({VXO}+1e-9)))/{ROUT}))
Bsrp vcc outp I = 0.5*(V(nicp)+sqrt(V(nicp)*V(nicp)+1e-12))
Bskp outp vee I = 0.5*(sqrt(V(nicp)*V(nicp)+1e-12)-V(nicp))
Bsrn vcc outn I = 0.5*(V(nicn)+sqrt(V(nicn)*V(nicn)+1e-12))
Bskn outn vee I = 0.5*(sqrt(V(nicn)*V(nicn)+1e-12)-V(nicn))
Iq   vcc vee DC {ICCQ}
Coutp outp 0 {COUT}
Coutn outn 0 {COUT}
* 100 Mohm noiseless leakage on each output: keeps the transient time step
* well-behaved when an output has no resistive load at all
Glkp outp 0 outp 0 1e-8
Glkn outn 0 outn 0 1e-8
.ends FDOPAMP_CORE

*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* FDOPAMP_FULL: the normal model (CM loop closed internally).
* Pass parameters as usual, e.g.  X1 ... FDOPAMP_FULL PARAMS: GBW=200Meg
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.subckt FDOPAMP_FULL inp inn vcc vee outp outn vocm
+ PARAMS:
+ A0=100k GBW=100Meg SR=200Meg FP2=300Meg FP3=1G
+ VOS=1m IB=2u IOS=0.1u
+ RID=1Meg CID=1p RIC=200Meg CIC=1p
+ CMRR=31.6k FCMRR=100k PSRRP=10k PSRRN=10k FPSRR=100k VCCN=5 VEEN=-5
+ VCMN={0.5*(VCCN+VEEN)}
+ ENOISE=5n FCEN=1k INOISE=1p FCIN=0
+ ICCQ=10m VHD=1.2 VLD=1.2 ICMHI=1.5 ICMLO=1 VK=0.1
+ ROUT=10 ISRC=50m ISNK=50m VXO=0 COUT=1p
+ VCLMP=100 RCLMP=100
+ A0CM=10k GBWCM=50Meg FPCM2=200Meg SRCM=100Meg VOSCM=1m
+ RVOCM=50k CVOCM=1p
Xc inp inn vcc vee outp outn vocm ncm ncm FDOPAMP_CORE PARAMS:
+ A0={A0} GBW={GBW} SR={SR} FP2={FP2} FP3={FP3}
+ VOS={VOS} IB={IB} IOS={IOS}
+ RID={RID} CID={CID} RIC={RIC} CIC={CIC}
+ CMRR={CMRR} FCMRR={FCMRR} PSRRP={PSRRP} PSRRN={PSRRN} FPSRR={FPSRR} VCCN={VCCN} VEEN={VEEN}
+ VCMN={VCMN}
+ ENOISE={ENOISE} FCEN={FCEN} INOISE={INOISE} FCIN={FCIN}
+ ICCQ={ICCQ} VHD={VHD} VLD={VLD} ICMHI={ICMHI} ICMLO={ICMLO} VK={VK}
+ ROUT={ROUT} ISRC={ISRC} ISNK={ISNK} VXO={VXO} COUT={COUT}
+ VCLMP={VCLMP} RCLMP={RCLMP}
+ A0CM={A0CM} GBWCM={GBWCM} FPCM2={FPCM2} SRCM={SRCM} VOSCM={VOSCM}
+ RVOCM={RVOCM} CVOCM={CVOCM}
.ends FDOPAMP_FULL
